# Local development only: todofy-core's local values. Copy to todofy/.dev.vars (gitignored; wrangler reads
# the .dev.vars next to wrangler.toml). Synthetic or your own test values only, never production keys.
#
# The committed wrangler.toml is production. Local dev uses local bindings only (never --remote) and D1
# commands always pass --local. The gateway is the primary of the combined process, so its local values go
# on the command line (docs/dev-notes.md §1):
#   uv run pywrangler dev -c gateway/wrangler.toml -c wrangler.toml \
#     --port 8787 --local-upstream todofy.localhost:8787 \
#     --var TODOFY_PUBLIC_HOST:todofy.localhost --var TODOFY_HOOKS_HOSTS:todofy-hooks.localhost \
#     --var BUILD_SHA:dev --var MAINTENANCE_MODE:false --var DEV_AUTH_BYPASS:true
#
# The runtime tests start their core from todofy/ as well, and this file overrides their core's vars: never
# put a switch (MAINTENANCE_MODE, PROCESSING_PAUSED, ...), BUILD_SHA or a timing knob here, and remove the
# file if a runtime test behaves unexpectedly. Unset, the switches CI adds at deploy read as false.
#
# The reminder links to the local owner UI (the same host the tests use).
TODOFY_PUBLIC_HOST=todofy.localhost
# Worker secrets, only to call the real upstreams from a local core:
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# TODOIST_API_KEY=
